# 2026-11-21, one Galaxy S26 sitting (campaign suffix qwen35-08b-mixed48-h1024): litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B's
# mixed 4/8-bit file Qwen3.5-0.8B_mixed48_h1024.litertlm (Hub commit 544ffe2ccf654a5e28f60d21f33db5c81899e961,
# 2026-11-20 21:18 UTC; 486,539,264 B, LFS sha256 61c65dbcaa86461184df1b60a82941c5d3e65fb535411d1b2192ccf222e98b35;
# the same bytes at the repo's main 7c656dc9, which changed only the README) on the protocol row,
# native-benchmark-1024x256 = litert_lm_advanced_main --benchmark, prefill forced to exactly 1024 tokens, decode 256,
# context 2048 (methodology/protocol-gemma4.md "The spec"), as the Galaxy S26 rows of the repo's int8 file
# (Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm) are written: the GPU row first, the CPU row after it.
# Both rows run the side build main-5dcf06020 (android/engine-pins.json: LiteRT-LM main 5dcf0602, 2026-11-20), not the
# flat pinned build: the file's metadata asks for LiteRT-LM 0.20.0 (min_runtime_version "0.20.0"), and no LiteRT-LM
# release was that new on 2026-11-21 (only nightly builds of 0.20.0 were out). LiteRT-LM main has shipped no prebuilt
# GPU accelerator since c57b9ae0 (2026-10-27), so the GPU row runs the accelerator compiled from source into that build
# (conditions.gpuAccelerator static-source): its GPU numbers are the source accelerator's, not those of the prebuilt one
# the v0.19.0-pregpu rows load (the ops/session-check/allow-list.tsv lines for this sitting's dirs).
# Model id litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B/mixed48_h1024 (ios/BenchmarkApp/Sources/Models/ModelCatalog.swift), so its
# cells stay apart from the int8 file's rows of litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B; the file is read from the Hugging Face
# cache snapshot of that commit (local=1).
# First row = the Android llama.cpp session anchor row of matrices/anchors.cells byte for byte (the payload's
# admission is judged on it, the primary anchor; the job's anchor phase runs both Android rows of anchors.cells
# before this file). No cooldown= (the runner's 120 s, the 0.6B / 1.7B class: docs/dashboard-cells-v1.md) and no
# runs= (the runner's default of 3 runs per row, round by round: GPU, CPU, GPU, CPU, GPU, CPU).
# Before the sitting, in the same hold: matrices/qwen35-08b-mixed48-h1024-s26-textcheck-main-android.cells (the
# reply text on this build, and one launch per backend that builds the caches beside the side build's link to the
# model, so that the sitting's runs are cache-loading runs, none of them firstEver).
# Estimate: under 35 min.
# Run while another process holds the phone (its pid in --hold-held-by; the job neither takes nor releases the hold):
#   BENCH_SITTING=1 python3 scripts/dashboard_job.py s26 --cells matrices/qwen35-08b-mixed48-h1024-s26-main-android.cells --suffix qwen35-08b-mixed48-h1024 --once --hold-held-by <keeper pid> --no-post
